WEBVTT

00:00:01.580 --> 00:00:03.180
Th-Things sure are quiet.

00:00:03.180 --> 00:00:04.080
Yep.

00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:08.110
<i>Neither one of us has caught anything yet.</i>

00:00:08.110 --> 00:00:10.940
<i>That means the first one to land a fish wins!</i>

00:00:10.940 --> 00:00:12.850
<i>I've been getting nibbles for a while now.</i>

00:00:12.850 --> 00:00:14.960
<i>But I can't reel them in.</i>

00:00:14.960 --> 00:00:17.140
<i>I need to throw him this bone.</i>

00:00:17.990 --> 00:00:21.750
<i>But it's too good of a fishing day to just sit on my hands.</i>

00:00:21.750 --> 00:00:24.960
<i>I want to come away with at least one fish!</i>

00:00:26.030 --> 00:00:28.660
<i>I can let him win by total count.</i>

00:00:28.660 --> 00:00:31.990
<i>After he catches one, then I'll hook a few.</i>

00:00:31.990 --> 00:00:33.990
<i>Now get a bite, Takamura-kun!</i>

00:00:33.990 --> 00:00:35.970
<i>I want to fish!</i>

00:00:37.970 --> 00:00:38.880
Got one!

00:00:38.880 --> 00:00:40.090
Congrats!

00:00:40.090 --> 00:00:42.790
Argh! It took the bait!

00:00:42.790 --> 00:00:45.310
Yeah, they can do that.

00:00:48.050 --> 00:00:49.460
Hell, yeah!

00:00:49.460 --> 00:00:53.060
What, again?! Bite the damn hook already!

00:00:54.670 --> 00:00:56.800
Were you about to say something?

00:00:56.800 --> 00:00:58.150
N-No.

00:01:00.400 --> 00:01:01.660
<i>It's biting!</i>

00:01:01.660 --> 00:01:03.920
<i>Hurry up and reel it in before it's too late!</i>

00:01:03.920 --> 00:01:05.500
Gotcha!

00:01:05.500 --> 00:01:07.430
Dammit, got away again!

00:01:07.430 --> 00:01:09.920
These fish sure know how to steal bait!

00:01:10.790 --> 00:01:13.460
<i>No, you suck way too hard!</i>

00:01:13.460 --> 00:01:15.520
S-Say something?

00:01:15.520 --> 00:01:17.430
N-No, I didn't.

00:01:19.680 --> 00:01:22.510
<i>Be patient, don't hook one yet.</i>

00:01:22.510 --> 00:01:24.680
<i>I have to give Takamura-kun this win!</i>

00:01:24.680 --> 00:01:27.470
<i>Looks like Yagi's completely lost his angler's luck,</i>

00:01:27.470 --> 00:01:29.690
<i>leaving me free to get the first bite!</i>

00:01:29.690 --> 00:01:31.690
<i>Don't hook one! Don't hook one!</i>

00:01:31.690 --> 00:01:33.690
<i>Hook one! Hook one! Hook one!</i>

00:01:33.690 --> 00:01:34.570
<i>Don't! Don't!</i>

00:01:34.570 --> 00:01:35.440
<i>Hook one! Hook one!</i>

00:01:35.440 --> 00:01:35.860
<i>Don't!</i>

00:01:35.860 --> 00:01:36.320
<i>Hook one!</i>

00:01:36.320 --> 00:01:36.700
<i>Don't!</i>

00:01:36.700 --> 00:01:37.110
<i>Hook one!</i>

00:01:37.110 --> 00:01:37.530
<i>Don't!</i>

00:01:37.530 --> 00:01:37.990
<i>Hook one!</i>

00:01:46.920 --> 00:01:48.890
They said this was the place.

00:01:48.890 --> 00:01:50.210
It is. Take a look!

00:01:50.210 --> 00:01:52.490
This sign actually says "No Yagis."

00:01:52.490 --> 00:01:55.310
What the hell did that old dude do?

00:01:55.310 --> 00:01:57.910
There's a new sign over here!

00:01:58.580 --> 00:01:59.990
There's something written on—

00:02:04.790 --> 00:02:07.540
Just what the heck did he do?

00:02:07.540 --> 00:02:10.420
Stop talking! I don't even want to imagine it!

00:02:11.020 --> 00:02:12.260
Takamura-san!

00:02:12.260 --> 00:02:13.470
Huh?

00:02:13.470 --> 00:02:15.050
Oh, welcome back!

00:02:15.670 --> 00:02:18.390
Why the hell are you acting so shocked?!{added "you"}

00:02:19.600 --> 00:02:21.270
He seems... happy.

00:02:21.270 --> 00:02:23.180
Did he actually win?

00:02:23.180 --> 00:02:24.520
It was a draw.

00:02:24.520 --> 00:02:26.600
They tied?!

00:02:26.600 --> 00:02:29.480
Yagi got three, Takamura got three.

00:02:29.480 --> 00:02:33.610
Neither had a good haul, so they decided to leave it at that.

00:02:33.610 --> 00:02:36.130
For Takamura-san, I'd say that's a great haul.

00:02:36.130 --> 00:02:37.740
So that's the fruits of his training?

00:02:37.740 --> 00:02:38.620
Thank goodness.

00:02:38.620 --> 00:02:40.910
But Yagi-san had only three?

00:02:40.910 --> 00:02:42.370
It's not like him.

00:02:45.730 --> 00:02:48.130
When Yagi-chan caught three fish,

00:02:48.130 --> 00:02:51.880
that's when Takamura dove in and grabbed three for himself.

00:02:51.880 --> 00:02:53.470
They were then escorted out.

00:02:53.470 --> 00:02:55.930
So he didn't use a pole?

00:02:55.930 --> 00:02:57.970
Well that explains the sign.

00:02:57.970 --> 00:03:02.100
What's the problem? As long as Takamura-san's happy!

00:03:02.100 --> 00:03:04.430
That's a weight off our shoulders!

00:03:04.430 --> 00:03:07.040
Who said you can relax?

00:03:08.300 --> 00:03:11.690
Your next matchups have been set.

00:03:12.570 --> 00:03:14.690
Besides Takamura-kun and Miyata-kun's matches,

00:03:14.690 --> 00:03:17.210
we've received the documents pertaining to you two's matches.

00:03:17.210 --> 00:03:18.520
Hell, yeah!

00:03:18.520 --> 00:03:21.700
Things are more real once we know who we're fighting.

00:03:21.700 --> 00:03:24.450
Are we up against some real bruisers?

00:03:24.450 --> 00:03:25.680
Indeed!

00:03:25.680 --> 00:03:29.710
You two will be fighting the Indonesian and Filipino national champions.

00:03:29.710 --> 00:03:32.560
Th-That's amazing! You'll be up against champions?

00:03:32.560 --> 00:03:34.030
I ain't afraid.

00:03:34.030 --> 00:03:37.220
We've both been through title matches.

00:03:37.840 --> 00:03:45.230
Kimura-kun will be facing the Filipino Junior Lightweight Champion, Eleki Battery.

00:03:49.520 --> 00:03:52.890
Who gave him that name? You're fighting an electronics store?{added "'re"}

00:03:52.890 --> 00:03:55.280
Who cares what his name is?!

00:03:55.280 --> 00:03:57.130
Aoki-kun will be fighting...

00:04:01.370 --> 00:04:04.370
the Indonesian Lightweight Champion.

00:04:05.030 --> 00:04:07.870
His name is Papaya Dachiu.

00:04:12.090 --> 00:04:14.760
Who cares what his name is?!

00:04:14.760 --> 00:04:16.370
I sure as hell do!

00:04:16.370 --> 00:04:19.090
"Papaya"? He sounds <i>real</i> tough to me!

00:04:19.090 --> 00:04:21.490
Don't laugh, Itagaki-kun!

00:04:21.490 --> 00:04:23.140
B-But...

00:04:23.140 --> 00:04:25.240
Fine, laugh if you want!

00:04:25.240 --> 00:04:27.100
But the actual fight will be no laughing matter!

00:04:27.100 --> 00:04:30.140
I'll split that Papaya in half!

00:04:30.140 --> 00:04:32.900
You best not take him lightly.

00:04:32.900 --> 00:04:36.150
The guy's a national champion, remember?

00:04:36.150 --> 00:04:41.200
But look at him! I ain't gonna lose to this dickhead!

00:04:41.200 --> 00:04:42.450
You won't?

00:04:42.450 --> 00:04:43.330
I ain't!

00:04:43.330 --> 00:04:44.230
You swear?

00:04:44.230 --> 00:04:45.660
Not in this lifetime!

00:04:45.660 --> 00:04:47.160
All right, then...

00:04:47.670 --> 00:04:51.210
this is your new hairdo if you lose.

00:05:01.430 --> 00:05:04.550
Kiss my ass! If I say I'm gonna win, I'm gonna win!

00:05:04.550 --> 00:05:06.180
Right! We got a deal!

00:05:06.180 --> 00:05:09.440
Careful out there. I hear he's got quite a punch.

00:05:10.110 --> 00:05:13.060
They call his right hand the "Coconut Punch."

00:05:13.060 --> 00:05:17.710
That's because his opponents thought they were being hit by coconuts.

00:05:17.710 --> 00:05:19.800
C-Coconuts?

00:05:20.320 --> 00:05:21.740
Do those hurt?

00:05:21.740 --> 00:05:23.370
Don't ask me!

00:05:23.370 --> 00:05:26.490
Do I look like I've been hit by those things?

00:05:26.490 --> 00:05:29.940
S-Senpai... I can't hold it in!

00:05:29.940 --> 00:05:32.210
My abs are about to burst open.

00:05:33.270 --> 00:05:36.460
As for you, Mr. Chucklehead...

00:05:36.680 --> 00:05:38.710
If you don't win,

00:05:38.710 --> 00:05:40.210
you got a makeover waiting!

00:05:48.770 --> 00:05:52.230
Bring it on, goddammit! I ain't gonna lose!

00:05:52.230 --> 00:05:56.790
Technically, Takamura-san, you yourself didn't beat Yagi-san today.

00:05:56.790 --> 00:05:58.370
Excuse me?

00:05:58.370 --> 00:06:03.260
And you cheated on top of it. So don't act like such a frickin' hotshot!

00:06:03.260 --> 00:06:06.380
You think you can beat Yagi, asshole?

00:06:06.380 --> 00:06:09.520
I will! How much you wanna bet?

00:06:11.750 --> 00:06:15.740
If I beat Yagi-san at fishing, that other bet is off!

00:06:15.740 --> 00:06:18.170
I ain't gonna do up my hair like any Papaya!

00:06:19.470 --> 00:06:23.160
<i>He doesn't think he can beat Papaya, does he?</i>

00:06:29.580 --> 00:06:32.810
<i>Only one more month until the match, huh?</i>

00:06:33.460 --> 00:06:37.150
<i>I'm not getting that 'do even if it kills me.</i>

00:06:37.150 --> 00:06:41.730
<i>And that son of a bitch Aoki came up with an escape clause.</i>

00:06:42.820 --> 00:06:45.880
<i>It looks like he's been practicing his ass off.</i>

00:06:45.880 --> 00:06:47.820
<i>Guess I can go see how he's doing.</i>

00:06:48.350 --> 00:06:49.830
Oh my god!

00:06:49.830 --> 00:06:53.020
You should definitely keep your current hairstyle!

00:06:53.020 --> 00:06:54.170
You said it, baby!

00:06:54.170 --> 00:06:57.270
I ain't getting that 'do for the life of me!

00:06:57.960 --> 00:07:00.280
But don't worry, you're on a roll!

00:07:00.280 --> 00:07:03.840
Yeah, I'm a natural when it comes to fishing!

00:07:03.840 --> 00:07:06.300
You're a natural when it comes to anything!

00:07:06.300 --> 00:07:08.340
You think so?

00:07:08.340 --> 00:07:09.600
I know so!

00:07:09.600 --> 00:07:10.510
Tomiko!

00:07:11.680 --> 00:07:15.030
Tomiko... Tomiko!

00:07:18.180 --> 00:07:20.990
<i>It looks like there won't be any fishing competition.</i>

00:07:22.280 --> 00:07:27.280
<i>Which means the only thing left for us... is to win our matches!</i>

00:07:30.640 --> 00:07:32.950
<i>I still gotta know,</i>

00:07:32.950 --> 00:07:35.150
<i>what the hell did that dumbass do anyway?</i>

00:07:40.730 --> 00:07:42.420
Those three are looking good.

00:07:43.280 --> 00:07:44.920
Especially that Takamura.

00:07:44.930 --> 00:07:48.470
He's powering through his training regimen with fire in his eyes.

00:07:48.870 --> 00:07:52.650
Even though he's back up to the middleweights like he should be,

00:07:52.650 --> 00:07:55.470
his weight management is still nothing to sneeze at.

00:07:57.020 --> 00:08:00.680
Building up your body is a fight against your own self.

00:08:00.680 --> 00:08:04.360
And Takamura's fight has just begun.

00:08:05.440 --> 00:08:06.550
Let's keep moving!

00:08:06.550 --> 00:08:07.280
Right!

00:08:08.320 --> 00:08:10.840
So can he really win two world titles?

00:08:10.840 --> 00:08:12.740
That we don't know.

00:08:12.740 --> 00:08:14.480
There has never been anybody...

00:08:14.480 --> 00:08:18.580
in the history of Japanese boxing who has ever won both the junior middle and the middleweights.

00:08:19.460 --> 00:08:26.540
He is truly setting foot in a territory where no Japanese man has gone before.

00:08:30.380 --> 00:08:31.510
Look at the poster!

00:08:31.990 --> 00:08:33.740
Now that looks nice!

00:08:33.740 --> 00:08:34.900
Mm-hmm!

00:08:34.900 --> 00:08:38.020
"A Passing Point," meaning crossroads.

00:08:38.530 --> 00:08:40.520
That's Takamura-kun's favorite word.

00:08:40.520 --> 00:08:44.990
I can't believe we know someone whose crossroads are at a second world title match.{is-are}

00:08:44.990 --> 00:08:46.690
We're so lucky!

00:08:47.220 --> 00:08:49.880
We might witness history in the making!

00:08:49.880 --> 00:08:51.640
I know we will.

00:08:51.640 --> 00:08:53.480
Takamura-san will pull through for us.

00:08:53.480 --> 00:08:55.410
He has to!

00:08:55.940 --> 00:08:59.240
David Eagle is a well-known champion even in America.

00:08:59.240 --> 00:09:01.920
It took a lot of money to lure him to Japan.

00:09:01.920 --> 00:09:07.960
If Takamura-kun doesn't nab that second title with blazing glory, we'll be deep in the red!

00:09:08.880 --> 00:09:11.350
Now that's what I call a buzzkill.

00:09:11.350 --> 00:09:11.980
Yeah.

00:09:11.980 --> 00:09:14.220
No need to fret!

00:09:14.680 --> 00:09:15.890
Guys!

00:09:15.890 --> 00:09:17.230
Welcome back!

00:09:17.750 --> 00:09:21.270
Getting that second title'll be easy as pie!

00:09:21.270 --> 00:09:25.480
I'll lure spectators from around the world and build you a new gym!

00:09:25.930 --> 00:09:28.820
Let's hope we're not counting chickens before they hatch.

00:09:28.820 --> 00:09:29.940
Can it.

00:09:30.490 --> 00:09:31.670
Oh?

00:09:31.670 --> 00:09:33.490
Now this is a nice poster.

00:09:33.490 --> 00:09:36.640
So we're fighting at Yokohama Arena?

00:09:36.640 --> 00:09:38.950
I'm always ready to fight!

00:09:39.630 --> 00:09:41.180
Time to exercise!

00:09:41.180 --> 00:09:41.960
Right!

00:09:45.880 --> 00:09:47.460
The fight's in the middle of the summer.

00:09:48.300 --> 00:09:53.430
Judging by the way he's sweating, we don't have to worry about his weight management.

00:09:53.430 --> 00:09:54.880
Yeah.

00:09:54.880 --> 00:09:56.440
<i>Actually, you're wrong.</i>

00:09:56.980 --> 00:10:00.620
<i>Takamura-san's weight management will be tough, even in the summer.</i>

00:10:01.850 --> 00:10:06.060
<i>He'll be forced to sweat buckets, yet he can't replenish fluids.</i>

00:10:06.060 --> 00:10:09.400
<i>In fact, he's in real danger of suffering dehydration.</i>

00:10:09.400 --> 00:10:12.650
<i>He'll feel constantly languid, and his body will feel heavy.</i>

00:10:13.990 --> 00:10:18.150
<i>Yet, he still has to run under the blazing sun.</i>

00:10:22.580 --> 00:10:24.210
Good, three minutes flat!

00:10:24.210 --> 00:10:25.830
You get one minute's rest!

00:10:26.830 --> 00:10:28.380
Need a towel?

00:10:30.040 --> 00:10:32.390
Not that I can see.

00:10:32.390 --> 00:10:36.590
Did you even sweat a drop under this hot sun?

00:10:37.340 --> 00:10:39.100
O... Old man....

00:10:39.510 --> 00:10:41.180
Don't force yourself to talk.

00:10:41.950 --> 00:10:44.720
Your overly chapped lips are bleeding.

00:10:47.740 --> 00:10:49.190
Happy now?

00:10:49.190 --> 00:10:50.980
What was that?

00:10:52.220 --> 00:10:56.450
You happy... you're getting... another belt?

00:11:00.790 --> 00:11:02.780
You're the one getting it.

00:11:02.780 --> 00:11:05.240
You're the one who's supposed to be happy about it.

00:11:05.240 --> 00:11:07.530
Don't expect me to be overjoyed about it.

00:11:09.790 --> 00:11:16.920
Still, the idea of seeing two world title belts side by side is marvelous indeed.

00:11:16.920 --> 00:11:22.060
I would like to see that before these old eyes become bleared with age.

00:11:31.940 --> 00:11:35.800
You got time to do that, then you should be running! Break's over!

00:11:45.970 --> 00:11:47.750
Fujii-san, here he is!

00:11:47.750 --> 00:11:48.080
Right.

00:11:51.040 --> 00:11:53.550
<i>Olympic gold medalist.</i>

00:11:53.550 --> 00:11:57.000
<i>Ever since turning pro, he's reached the top of the world after only 15 fights,</i>

00:11:57.000 --> 00:11:58.840
<i>never knowing a loss.</i>

00:11:59.710 --> 00:12:03.240
<i>His career has been one constant, triumphant victory lap.</i>

00:12:03.240 --> 00:12:05.310
<i>He is truly the Golden Eagle.</i>

00:12:07.830 --> 00:12:10.760
<i>WBC World Middleweight Champion,</i>

00:12:10.760 --> 00:12:12.610
<i>David "Golden" Eagle.</i>

00:12:12.610 --> 00:12:14.120
David, may we have a moment?

00:12:14.120 --> 00:12:15.720
We have some questions for you.

00:12:16.770 --> 00:12:18.020
Sure thing.

00:12:21.370 --> 00:12:24.620
You are a highly celebrated boxer in your own country.

00:12:24.620 --> 00:12:28.340
Why would you deign to set foot in enemy territory?

00:12:28.340 --> 00:12:30.150
That's what I want to know.

00:12:30.840 --> 00:12:34.090
Do you all remember Brian Hawk?

00:12:34.210 --> 00:12:35.460
Hawk?

00:12:35.460 --> 00:12:37.170
Yes, of course.

00:12:37.170 --> 00:12:40.590
I once considered him my most powerful foe.

00:12:41.090 --> 00:12:45.640
But then, I received the shocking news that he lost.

00:12:45.640 --> 00:12:48.990
There is a very strong man in this tiny island nation.

00:12:48.990 --> 00:12:51.340
My thoughts of him even kept me up at night.

00:12:51.340 --> 00:12:53.240
Then that's when you got the offer?

00:12:53.240 --> 00:12:54.110
Yes!

00:12:54.110 --> 00:12:56.470
I came to Japan,

00:12:56.470 --> 00:13:00.150
because I want to see this Mamoru Takamura. That's all.

00:13:00.570 --> 00:13:02.660
That's a very simplistic reason.

00:13:03.330 --> 00:13:05.410
Is it really all there is to it?

00:13:05.410 --> 00:13:08.690
They have your dinner waiting at the hotel.

00:13:08.690 --> 00:13:10.920
No, take me directly to the gym.

00:13:11.500 --> 00:13:14.430
I've sat too long on that plane.

00:13:14.430 --> 00:13:17.920
I want to get back to my fighting rhythm as soon as possible.

00:13:18.410 --> 00:13:20.980
He's not even thinking about resting or sightseeing.

00:13:20.980 --> 00:13:24.680
It appears he's indeed focused only on Takamura.

00:13:24.680 --> 00:13:29.180
He and Brian Hawk are totally different boxers.

00:13:29.180 --> 00:13:32.650
He knows only glory, but doesn't bask in it.

00:13:33.270 --> 00:13:36.360
The ultimate workhorse who never relies on just his natural gifts.

00:13:37.570 --> 00:13:41.070
A real champion has landed.

00:13:45.780 --> 00:13:48.950
So this public sparring starts at two?

00:13:48.950 --> 00:13:52.610
Yeah, I want to see exactly who we're facing.

00:13:53.910 --> 00:13:57.230
So, why are you following us?

00:14:00.780 --> 00:14:05.200
This thing is being held at Miyata's Kawahara Gym, I suppose.

00:14:09.600 --> 00:14:12.070
What's with the crowd?

00:14:12.600 --> 00:14:14.650
That's David Eagle-san!

00:14:14.650 --> 00:14:17.030
What's he doing with all those kids?

00:14:17.780 --> 00:14:20.600
Hey there, little guy, come over here!

00:14:20.600 --> 00:14:22.700
Why don't I give you an autograph?

00:14:22.700 --> 00:14:24.190
M-Me?

00:14:24.190 --> 00:14:26.360
No, I couldn't possibly...

00:14:26.360 --> 00:14:29.580
I-I'm with your opponent... and we're here, you know, to scout...

00:14:32.710 --> 00:14:35.420
S-Sankyuu berry machee! {Sounds delicious}

00:14:35.420 --> 00:14:37.540
I made a memory!

00:14:37.540 --> 00:14:39.620
Don't get elated over getting his autograph!

00:14:39.620 --> 00:14:43.400
Still, did he even schedule a signing session?

00:14:43.400 --> 00:14:45.720
He does that by his own volition.

00:14:46.430 --> 00:14:47.870
Miyata-kun!

00:14:47.870 --> 00:14:50.350
Those are just the neighborhood kids.

00:14:51.280 --> 00:14:56.350
But he says that some of them may be thinking of going to the Olympics or turning pro.

00:14:57.190 --> 00:15:01.860
He hopes that his presence can inspire at least one of them to go down that path.

00:15:02.330 --> 00:15:05.360
Now there's an exemplary athlete.

00:15:05.360 --> 00:15:09.880
S-So he thought I was another neighborhood kid?

00:15:09.880 --> 00:15:14.370
Those foreigners think we all look young. {TRUE FACT!!!}

00:15:14.370 --> 00:15:17.120
I think the sparring is about to start.

00:15:23.640 --> 00:15:24.800
Next partner.

00:15:24.800 --> 00:15:25.880
Yeah!

00:15:30.970 --> 00:15:33.380
All of his punches are high level,

00:15:33.380 --> 00:15:35.980
but his one-two punch is something else.

00:15:35.980 --> 00:15:39.010
It'll be a tough fight for Takamura if he keeps taking those.

00:15:39.010 --> 00:15:40.840
Color me surprised.

00:15:40.840 --> 00:15:42.030
I agree.

00:15:42.030 --> 00:15:45.540
He's putting everything out there in the open.

00:15:45.540 --> 00:15:49.070
Does he have brass ones, or is he deliberately throwing down the gauntlet?

00:15:49.070 --> 00:15:53.580
<i>I see this champion wants to fight Takamura head on.</i>

00:15:53.990 --> 00:15:56.440
<i>I'm really glad we get to see the real boxer in action.</i>

00:15:56.440 --> 00:15:58.580
<i>That shows the guy is worth fighting.</i>

00:16:03.240 --> 00:16:05.110
H-He's good!

00:16:06.530 --> 00:16:11.930
He gives 100% during training and is kind to foreign kids.

00:16:11.930 --> 00:16:14.180
It's like he's a superhero.

00:16:15.010 --> 00:16:18.300
He's probably the type of guy Takamura-san hates the most.

00:16:18.300 --> 00:16:20.830
He does get easily peeved.

00:16:20.830 --> 00:16:24.230
We're talking about his boxing style, not his personality.

00:16:25.320 --> 00:16:29.840
The only people who I believe can overcome Takamura-san's unconventional style are orthodox boxers.

00:16:30.830 --> 00:16:32.690
He'll be in for a tough fight.

00:16:33.520 --> 00:16:35.700
Can Takamura-san win?

00:16:35.700 --> 00:16:40.420
I can't make any predictions, but I know the match will be epic.

00:16:41.150 --> 00:16:44.420
Oh, and how are you doing, Miyata-kun?

00:16:44.420 --> 00:16:47.340
Why would I be in anything but tip-top shape?

00:16:47.880 --> 00:16:49.780
Y-Yeah, you're right.

00:16:49.780 --> 00:16:52.830
Actually, I'm not sure.

00:16:52.830 --> 00:16:54.880
I'm trying to work on something new.

00:16:54.880 --> 00:16:56.720
Something new?

00:16:56.720 --> 00:16:58.190
Let's hope that...

00:16:58.810 --> 00:17:02.190
just like you revealed your new move in the Sawamura fight,

00:17:03.210 --> 00:17:07.690
I won't hesitate to put everything on the line.

00:17:14.590 --> 00:17:19.750
Kid! What do you, as an active boxer, think of David Eagle?

00:17:20.160 --> 00:17:22.110
He's like a superhero.

00:17:22.680 --> 00:17:24.930
Even though he's supposed to be our foe,

00:17:24.930 --> 00:17:30.760
he's the man I could picture standing on top of the world, representing our hopes and dreams.

00:17:30.760 --> 00:17:32.900
A superhero, eh?

00:17:32.900 --> 00:17:37.340
I agree that he's a wonderful athlete who takes training seriously.

00:17:38.080 --> 00:17:41.770
He doesn't have Takamura beaten on that account.

00:17:45.990 --> 00:17:48.030
I've had enough of you little shits!

00:17:48.030 --> 00:17:49.580
Give us an autograph!

00:17:49.580 --> 00:17:51.950
Why? We were going to cheer for you!

00:17:58.290 --> 00:17:59.740
Get lost, punks!

00:18:01.280 --> 00:18:04.430
H-He kicked, punched, and chased them away.

00:18:04.430 --> 00:18:05.570
He's a monster.

00:18:05.570 --> 00:18:07.090
He's hell's emissary.

00:18:07.800 --> 00:18:10.820
I know weight management makes you irritable,

00:18:10.820 --> 00:18:13.090
but what you did just now...

00:18:14.130 --> 00:18:16.170
<i>I better back away...</i>

00:18:17.300 --> 00:18:19.150
What the hell is this on your back?!

00:18:19.150 --> 00:18:20.850
Are you on his side now?!

00:18:22.840 --> 00:18:26.260
I don't believe you!  I don't believe you!

00:18:23.830 --> 00:18:25.380
{overlap}What did I do?!

00:18:25.380 --> 00:18:27.190
{overlap}Why are you chasing me!

00:18:26.260 --> 00:18:28.980
I don't believe you!

00:18:30.770 --> 00:18:34.530
I hear that Kamogawa Gym will not do any public sparrings.

00:18:34.530 --> 00:18:36.950
But we went ahead and showed our entire arsenal.

00:18:39.880 --> 00:18:46.460
Well, it appears our opponent would rather take a rest from his weight management rather than spar.

00:18:46.460 --> 00:18:49.250
You should rest up, too.

00:18:49.250 --> 00:18:53.330
You're putting so much into this, it's starting to make us worry.

00:18:53.840 --> 00:18:57.850
There's no such thing as "putting in too much" against Mamoru Takamura.

00:18:57.850 --> 00:19:01.850
In fact, I worry that I didn't do enough.

00:19:02.600 --> 00:19:07.310
You've seen for yourself how much Brian Hawk has changed.

00:19:08.810 --> 00:19:10.980
<i>Hawk, I have to know!</i>

00:19:11.430 --> 00:19:14.120
<i>I can't believe you lost.</i>

00:19:14.120 --> 00:19:15.990
<i>How did that happen?</i>

00:19:15.990 --> 00:19:19.300
<i>Get out. Before I kill you.</i>

00:19:19.300 --> 00:19:21.490
<i>Weren't you feeling well? Or was...</i>

00:19:21.490 --> 00:19:24.910
<i>that Mamoru Takamura that strong of a fighter?</i>

00:19:25.950 --> 00:19:27.550
<i>Go to hell!</i>

00:19:27.550 --> 00:19:30.670
<i>Don't you dare mention his name!</i>

00:19:30.670 --> 00:19:34.670
<i>Don't you ever talk about him in front of me!</i>

00:19:34.670 --> 00:19:37.090
<i>Tell me, Hawk! Is he...</i>

00:19:37.090 --> 00:19:38.140
<i>Stop!</i>

00:19:40.640 --> 00:19:44.810
<i>How could a man like Hawk become so damaged?</i>

00:19:45.360 --> 00:19:48.420
<i>I want to know exactly how strong he is.</i>

00:19:51.180 --> 00:19:54.070
I don't want to merely see him spar.

00:19:54.440 --> 00:19:58.510
I want to experience the man named Mamoru Takamura.

00:19:59.270 --> 00:20:03.950
I'm only interested in how strong he is... inside the ring.
